From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:05:18 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Keep the format in the sub-device state

The driver kept the active format in its own structure behind its own
mutex, which predates the sub-device state API. That leaves get_fmt
having to special case TRY versus ACTIVE, and it means nothing can look
at the active format from a context that already holds a lock.

Move the format into the sub-device state and add an .init_state that
seeds it, so the generic v4l2_subdev_get_fmt() can serve get_fmt. The
state lock becomes the control handler lock, which is what lets a
control callback reach the active format directly - the timing controls
in a later patch need exactly that.

The private mutex goes away with it. The frame interval callbacks are
handed an already locked state by the core, so they must not lock again.

Also drop a dead #if 0 block in set_frame_interval() that referenced a
register define which has never existed for this sensor.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
